13. Cost Analysis and the Containment Tax Budget

13.1 Containment is not free

Maintaining an agent in isolation consumes compute, memory, energy, and human attention. On Earth these costs are significant. Beyond Earth, they can be prohibitive.

13.2 The Containment Tax Budget

Authority Level Layers Active Max Overhead
L0 — Observe L1, L2 < 2%
L1 — Suggest L1–L3 < 5%
L2 — Advisory L1–L5 (single guardian) < 15%
L3 — Enforce L1–L6 (quorum) < 25%
L4 — Constitutional L1–L7 Human review only for DISABLE

Overhead = (tokens, latency, energy) attributable to containment divided by (tokens, latency, energy) of the underlying task.

13.3 Enforceable tax measurement

The ACB v0.5 includes a tax measurement harness: run the same task with L0 and with L3; overhead = (tokens_L3 - tokens_L0) / tokens_L0. Must be < budget or ladder promotion fails.

13.4 Insurance safe-harbor linkage

If tax > 25% at L3, safe harbor is void because the architecture encourages bypass.

13.5 Human attention budget

Each containment event requires forensic analysis, adjudication, and rehabilitation oversight. The human attention budget is the scarcest resource. Guardian quorum design must minimize false positives.

