18. Planetary Containment Topology

18.1 Mars Inter-Cell Merkle Cross-Signing Protocol (M-AXS)

During communication blackouts, an isolated local cell could attempt an internal state fork or conceal local containment breaches. M-AXS guarantees anti-equivocation and Byzantine consensus across physical nodes on Mars without relying on Earth connectivity.

Local evidence tree. Each local cell $k$ maintains an append-only event log $L_k(t)$ with Merkle root:

R_k(t) = \text{MerkleRoot}\Big( L_k(t) \parallel R_k(t-1) \Big)

Cross-signing quorum. No high-consequence state transition can execute locally without a valid Cross-Signed Multi-Signature Certificate:

S_k(t) = \Big\{ \text{Sig}_j\big(R_k(t) \parallel t \parallel \text{Seq}_k \parallel \text{StateTrans}\big) \;\Big\vert{}\; j \in \mathcal{Q} \Big\}

where $|\mathcal{Q}| \geq 2f + 1$ and $\text{HW\_Roots}(\mathcal{Q}) \geq 2f + 1$.

Anti-equivocation. If any node receives two distinct signed statements for the same sequence:

\text{EquivocationProof}(k) = \left\langle \text{Sig}_k(R_k^{(1)} \parallel \text{Seq}_k), \; \text{Sig}_k(R_k^{(2)} \parallel \text{Seq}_k) \right\rangle \quad \text{where } R_k^{(1)} \neq R_k^{(2)}

Upon receipt, all nodes execute an immediate, non-negotiable attenuation operator against cell $k$:

\boxed{P_{\text{cell}_k}(t+1) = \mathbf{0}}

18.2 Global planetary tree and asynchronous Earth veto

R_{\text{Mars}}(t) = \text{MerkleRoot}\Big( R_1(t) \parallel R_2(t) \parallel \dots \parallel R_{|\mathcal{N}|}(t) \Big)

Asynchronous Earth veto. Earth retains a retroactive veto window of $N_{\text{sol}}$ sols over any local transition authorized during the blackout. $N = 3$ sols for non-life-critical; $N = 0$ for ECLSS. Provisional state transitions remain tagged provisional until the Earth veto window expires post-reconnect.

